1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,810
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,480
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,080
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:10,850
That's why I said to find
the cheapest place.

5
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:14,450
Don't bother considering
safety or infrastructure.

6
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:15,750
Just find the cheapest option.

7
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:19,590
Study abroad or not, she's an adult.

8
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:23,560
Just cut corners.

9
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:30,870
Seriously.

10
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:34,810
Why do I have to deal with this crap
all because of Ko Eun Seol?

11
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:44,780
For someone...

12
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:49,520
Someone like Ko Eun Seol?

13
00:00:54,830 --> 00:00:56,860
Is that how Director Joo
truly feels?

14
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:03,600
Wait, then everything
she said to me...

15
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:07,110
Was it all a lie?

16
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:27,360
Eun Seol, the study abroad agency
just called.

17
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:29,760
I think you'll really like it.

18
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:31,930
Shall we discuss it
over dinner tomorrow?

19
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:51,250
Hae Ra,

20
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,490
I'm your dad.

21
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:59,320
I'll call the police.
Get lost right now.

22
00:01:59,890 --> 00:02:02,660
Right, you must be pretty surprised.

23
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:05,530
Here, take a look at this first.

24
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:12,970
(Paternity Test Results:
An Guk Cheol, Kang Hae Ra)

25
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,640
(A 99.999 percent genetic match)

26
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:19,010
You crazy bum,
who are you trying to scam?

27
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:21,910
How's this for proof?

28
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:33,190
Director Joo?

29
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:36,530
She's Mom to you now,
not Director Joo.

30
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:41,800
What kind of nonsense is this?
Stop being so cryptic.

31
00:02:41,970 --> 00:02:44,500
You aren't Kang Hae Ra,
you're An Hae Ra.

32
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:47,410
Also, I'm your dad,

33
00:02:47,610 --> 00:02:51,340
and your mom is Joo Mi Ran,
or rather, Joo Ae Sook.

34
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:57,320
- You're crazy.
- If you still can't believe me,

35
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:00,490
take a strand of Ae Sook's hair
and get it tested.

36
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:08,460
Your dad will be waiting
for you, Hae Ra.

37
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:29,710
What the...

38
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,420
- Hey.
- Did you get home safe?

39
00:03:40,190 --> 00:03:41,290
Yes. And you, Seok Jin?

40
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:42,960
I made it back fine too.

41
00:03:43,630 --> 00:03:44,630
Tired, right?

42
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:46,930
I am.

43
00:03:47,730 --> 00:03:49,330
I forgot to drop off the gifts
for your parents.

44
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,600
Should we drive home together
after work tomorrow?

45
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:55,310
Don't bother.
I'll make sure they get them.

46
00:03:57,110 --> 00:03:59,510
Right, sure. Get some rest then.

47
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,280
You too.

48
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:39,950
I'm a bit tired tonight.

49
00:04:54,370 --> 00:04:55,770
Wait, isn't this Swerang?

50
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,200
How did you know I like this brand?

51
00:04:58,270 --> 00:05:00,440
Wait. These are from Swerang.

52
00:05:00,770 --> 00:05:03,040
A few years back,
this came out as a VIP exclusive.

53
00:05:03,170 --> 00:05:05,040
Was it capped at
around 100 people or so?

54
00:05:06,110 --> 00:05:08,680
Anyway, where did you get this,
Eun Seol?

55
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:10,010
Is it the real deal?

56
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:13,550
Then this...

57
00:05:15,020 --> 00:05:16,350
Are they Director Joo's?

58
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:24,830
Mom, why are you walking like that?

59
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:29,370
I haven't worn nice heels
in a while,

60
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:31,300
and my feet are killing me.

61
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:33,770
The shoes from the engagement party
were uncomfortable, weren't they?

62
00:05:34,910 --> 00:05:37,380
Yes, even my toenails hurt.

63
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:40,310
This won't do.

64
00:05:42,250 --> 00:05:43,250
Is that better?

65
00:05:43,850 --> 00:05:44,980
Much better.

66
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:48,550
Why didn't you say so at the party
instead of keeping it to yourself?

67
00:05:48,550 --> 00:05:49,820
I feel awful.

68
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:53,860
As long as you're happy,
I'm totally fine.

69
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:56,490
Mr. Seok Jin.

70
00:05:56,930 --> 00:05:59,060
- Yes?
- You're happy now, right?

71
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,600
What?

72
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:05,670
Now that you're engaged to Hae Ra,
you're happy.

73
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:12,940
Mom, want to go shoe shopping
during lunch today?

74
00:06:13,610 --> 00:06:15,080
Wait, really?

75
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:22,020
This is the store I opened.

76
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:24,420
You were bummed
you couldn't come last time, right?

77
00:06:24,890 --> 00:06:25,890
Yes.

78
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:29,630
There are so many
pretty and cool shoes.

79
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,360
How about trying on
some comfortable sneakers today?

80
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,100
Okay.

81
00:06:34,470 --> 00:06:35,470
Have a seat.

82
00:06:36,530 --> 00:06:38,800
Since your knees usually hurt,

83
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,010
you need something comfortable.

84
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:47,450
This just came out. Try this one on.

85
00:06:48,010 --> 00:06:49,180
Okay.

86
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:53,150
Let's put these on
and take a walk together.

87
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:58,220
I can put it on myself.

88
00:07:02,730 --> 00:07:05,660
All right. Try walking.
We need to see if it's comfortable.

89
00:07:07,770 --> 00:07:11,300
I love it. It's so comfortable.
Isn't it pretty?

90
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:12,470
It's pretty.

91
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:16,940
Mr. Seok Jin, I want to keep
these on and go for that walk.

92
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:22,110
You're back.

93
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:48,910
Boss,

94
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,510
let's eat at my house today.

95
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,240
What?

96
00:07:54,250 --> 00:07:58,450
I thought having my dad's cooking
might cheer you up.

97
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:01,050
What do you mean by that?

98
00:08:01,350 --> 00:08:02,950
Whenever people eat
my dad's cooking,

99
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:05,190
they can't stop laughing.

100
00:08:06,890 --> 00:08:08,390
That's ridiculous.

101
00:08:09,090 --> 00:08:10,490
You don't believe me?

102
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:14,070
Join us for dinner, then.
You'll see what I mean.

103
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:22,370
By the way, Eun Seol,

104
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:24,710
did you find out
if those gloves are authentic?

105
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:26,940
Why are you so curious about that?

106
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:29,250
Because they're
a true limited edition.

107
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:32,250
I actually have a knockoff myself.

108
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:34,020
- A knockoff?
- Yes.

109
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:36,290
It's already lunchtime.

110
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:37,790
It sure is.

111
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:40,690
Didn't Ms. Kang say
she was coming in today?

112
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:44,530
She's the Cheongma heiress.
She comes and goes as she pleases.

113
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:46,660
Eun Seol,

114
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:48,300
care to join us for lunch?

115
00:08:49,670 --> 00:08:52,270
Go on ahead. I'll eat later.

116
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:53,940
What do you want to eat?

117
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:56,240
Let's just hit the cafeteria.

118
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:58,210
- How about burgers?
- Burgers?

119
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:05,550
Should I go to the store myself?

120
00:09:08,790 --> 00:09:09,890
You're here.

121
00:09:23,270 --> 00:09:24,440
If you still can't believe me,

122
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,710
take a strand of Ae Sook's hair
and get it tested.

123
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:45,620
So you checked
all the gambling arcades...

124
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:47,260
and gambling dens in Seoul?

125
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:48,290
Yes.

126
00:09:48,690 --> 00:09:51,100
I hired private investigators
and detectives,

127
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:53,660
but he vanished into thin air
this time.

128
00:09:55,430 --> 00:09:58,100
The moment you find him,
lock him up in a hospital.

129
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:00,170
Yes, I'll do that.

130
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,140
Hire more people.

131
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:04,340
I don't care how much it costs.

132
00:10:05,210 --> 00:10:06,210
Understood.

133
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,390
What about our daughter?

134
00:10:17,990 --> 00:10:20,460
I heard you gave birth
to our daughter.

135
00:10:23,430 --> 00:10:26,200
She died a very long time ago.

136
00:10:29,370 --> 00:10:30,370
Don't you dare.

137
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:33,270
Lay one finger on my daughter
and see what happens.

138
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:34,970
The moment you do,

139
00:10:34,970 --> 00:10:36,840
I'll destroy you with my own hands.

140
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:44,980
Imperial...

141
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:47,350
S900.

142
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:53,590
Since my daughter will soon be
the successor of Cheongma Group,

143
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:56,630
I should at least drive
a luxury import.

144
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:58,860
And as for a home,

145
00:10:59,630 --> 00:11:03,030
a 165m² place
overlooking the Han River.

146
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:09,440
To keep up appearances
for my Hae Ra,

147
00:11:09,510 --> 00:11:12,480
I should dress head-to-toe
in luxury designer brands, right?

148
00:11:15,010 --> 00:11:16,280
(My Daughter)

149
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:20,350
Yes, of course.
Your dad is right here.

150
00:11:22,290 --> 00:11:23,450
My daughter.

151
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:24,890
Were you looking for your dad?

152
00:11:25,190 --> 00:11:26,260
Let's meet.

153
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:30,430
Of course. Where do you want
your dad to go, Princess?

154
00:11:33,230 --> 00:11:34,370
What the...

155
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:40,640
(My Daughter)

156
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:41,970
(7:30 p.m., Cafe Hyerang)

157
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:52,150
Do you think
I believe a word you say?

158
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:55,990
Did you think you could fool me
with a scrap of paper and a photo?

159
00:11:56,290 --> 00:11:59,420
It's not about fooling you.
You're finally learning the truth.

160
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,890
Also, your mom only hid it
for your sake,

161
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,830
so don't hold it against her.

162
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:06,560
Watch your mouth!
Who are you calling my mom?

163
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,330
My mom...

164
00:12:08,570 --> 00:12:11,100
is Chairman Kim Jung Sun
of Cheongma Scholarship Foundation.

165
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,540
Oh, please.
She's your adoptive mother.

166
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:15,110
Your birth mother
is Joo Mi Ran, no...

167
00:12:15,270 --> 00:12:16,540
I mean, Joo Ae Sook.

168
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:23,050
What's your relationship
with Director Joo?

169
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,520
Who do you think you are...

170
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:29,250
to threaten me like this?

171
00:12:30,890 --> 00:12:33,490
I'm Joo Ae Sook's husband,
and your father.

172
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:36,560
She switched you into that family
and raised you there.

173
00:12:37,230 --> 00:12:39,460
Daughter, do you still not get it?

174
00:12:40,870 --> 00:12:42,200
Did you inherit my brains?

175
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:46,840
I was switched?

176
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,370
That's it.

177
00:12:48,370 --> 00:12:52,080
Ae Sook has always been
terrifyingly good at scheming.

178
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:53,580
With no father in the picture,

179
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,210
she must've been terrified
of raising you alone.

180
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:58,880
But pulling a clever stunt
like this?

181
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:03,090
I really had no idea
she'd switch you into a rich family.

182
00:13:03,150 --> 00:13:04,160
Shut it!

183
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:06,360
From the beginning,

184
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:08,330
I've been the only daughter
of Cheongma Group.

185
00:13:09,930 --> 00:13:11,600
Maybe because the weather
has been so warm,

186
00:13:11,730 --> 00:13:13,560
the mosquitoes are out
buzzing around again.

187
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:14,900
In our family,

188
00:13:15,430 --> 00:13:17,300
mosquitoes have eaten us alive
for generations.

189
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,700
Isn't it the same for you?

190
00:13:23,410 --> 00:13:24,880
That's...

191
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:27,110
If you take after me,
you must've suffered...

192
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:29,250
from ingrown toenails as a kid.

193
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:34,050
Anyway, enough about that.

194
00:13:37,050 --> 00:13:39,660
If you still can't believe it,
run a test against this.

195
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:43,690
(Korea Genetic Analysis Institute)

196
00:13:53,570 --> 00:13:56,210
Anyway, Hae Ra, I'll get going.

197
00:13:56,270 --> 00:13:58,410
Call me if there's anything else
you want to know.

198
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:02,050
Darn it.

199
00:14:02,850 --> 00:14:05,620
Your mom must miss me like crazy.

200
00:14:20,630 --> 00:14:21,630
Eun Seol.

201
00:14:22,530 --> 00:14:25,000
Before the semester starts
at design school,

202
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,000
how about heading abroad early?

203
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:29,370
Before the semester starts?

204
00:14:29,670 --> 00:14:30,810
That's right.

205
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:34,080
Going early
gives you time to adjust,

206
00:14:34,310 --> 00:14:36,210
and it'd be good to get used
to speaking English beforehand.

207
00:14:38,950 --> 00:14:40,850
I'll think about it.

208
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:43,220
I narrowed down
a few studio apartments.

209
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,190
Did you tell your family?

210
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:49,360
No. I haven't told them yet.

211
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:52,660
I want to think a bit more
about moving out too.

212
00:14:53,630 --> 00:14:55,130
Until I go study abroad,

213
00:14:55,630 --> 00:14:58,440
part of me thinks
I should just stay at home.

214
00:14:59,070 --> 00:15:00,070
I see.

215
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:05,780
I get it.
You must have a lot on your mind.

216
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:07,710
Take your time.

217
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:11,280
Of course I want you
to move out of that house,

218
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,980
but I don't want to force you.

219
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:16,450
As long as you're comfortable,
I'm all for it.

220
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,360
Thank you.

221
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:23,090
But you have to promise me
you'll study abroad.

222
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:27,930
In my opinion,
there's a right time for studying.

223
00:15:28,370 --> 00:15:31,540
If you put it off any longer,
it won't be easy to go.

224
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,910
It looks like Hae Ra
went straight to work...

225
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,580
after getting back from her trip.

226
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:43,410
I know.

227
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:45,050
Did getting engaged...

228
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,420
make her grow up a bit?

229
00:15:46,850 --> 00:15:48,650
They say married couples
become alike.

230
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:52,320
Hae Ra must be picking up
Chief Cha's diligent nature.

231
00:15:54,490 --> 00:15:55,960
Once Chief Cha and Hae Ra
get married,

232
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,700
what do you want to do?

233
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,230
About what?

234
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:03,000
Why don't we have Chief Cha
move into our house?

235
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,840
Then what about So Yeon?

236
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:08,210
We'll move her into a facility
when the time is right.

237
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:12,210
So Yeon isn't in a state
where she needs a facility's help.

238
00:16:12,410 --> 00:16:14,080
Chief Cha won't like it either.

239
00:16:14,510 --> 00:16:16,150
Well, Hae Ra's busy.

240
00:16:16,210 --> 00:16:19,350
You also have your hands full
with the scholarship foundation.

241
00:16:19,650 --> 00:16:20,920
For So Yeon too,

242
00:16:21,250 --> 00:16:23,750
a facility might actually provide
more stability.

243
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:25,790
That's true, but...

244
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:27,420
You remember, don't you?

245
00:16:27,660 --> 00:16:30,490
I also started out
living with my in-laws.

246
00:16:31,230 --> 00:16:32,800
Your father always said...

247
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,970
that to become
a true part of Cheongma,

248
00:16:35,100 --> 00:16:37,330
you have to start
under the family's roof.

249
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:38,400
I know.

250
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:43,640
My dad wanted you to be reborn
as a true Cheongma man.

251
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:48,380
Still, Chief Cha
probably won't like it.

252
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,750
I'll have to persuade him.

253
00:16:57,690 --> 00:17:00,620
You haven't been taking
your vitamins regularly, have you?

254
00:17:00,690 --> 00:17:01,830
Oh, right.

255
00:17:02,690 --> 00:17:04,530
I'll make sure
you don't forget to take them.

256
00:17:18,710 --> 00:17:20,010
Should I take some too?

257
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:22,480
Sure. Here, let me give you yours.

258
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:26,850
Kang Young Hoon...

259
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:30,450
He's definitely hiding something.

260
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:34,020
He was a warm person.

261
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:37,030
He was also extremely good
at his job.

262
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:40,530
That's why even
the former chairman of Cheongma...

263
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:43,700
was really fond of my husband.

264
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:46,170
The former chairman of Cheongma?

265
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:50,370
Yes.
He got promoted really fast, too.

266
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:55,280
He must have been
remarkably talented.

267
00:17:55,410 --> 00:17:56,750
Of course.

268
00:17:57,450 --> 00:18:00,920
So he had a lot of jealous friends.

269
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:04,620
Hae Ra's dad was pretty sulky
about it.

270
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:09,160
If I dig into Oh Tae Seop,
who killed Chief Cha's father,

271
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:11,660
something might turn up.

272
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:21,540
Wait, a culinary master
like you, Mi Rae,

273
00:18:21,710 --> 00:18:24,310
wanted to eat my cooking?

274
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:27,740
Yes. Dad, your cooking
makes people laugh.

275
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:29,850
What? Laugh? In what way?

276
00:18:29,850 --> 00:18:32,120
Laugh, my foot.

277
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:34,350
What's funny
about messing with food?

278
00:18:34,450 --> 00:18:37,250
That's the funny part,
which is why I invited my boss.

279
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:39,120
- Can I eat some too?
- Hold on.

280
00:18:40,090 --> 00:18:42,090
This might not be suitable
for minors.

281
00:18:42,630 --> 00:18:45,300
This dish has an age restriction.

282
00:18:48,470 --> 00:18:50,630
Here, boss, you go first.

283
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:52,600
No, elders should eat first.

284
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:54,810
No way. I'm good.

285
00:18:54,870 --> 00:18:56,510
Go ahead and dig in,
Teun Teun's mom.

286
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:58,740
Then, I'll enjoy the food.

287
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:12,890
Wait, how is this
spicy stir-fried squid?

288
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:15,660
No, seriously,
it tastes like alien squid.

289
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:17,790
See? What did I tell you?

290
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:20,400
I told you it's impossible
not to laugh.

291
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:21,870
I want some too.

292
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:23,430
Not you. It'll upset your stomach.

293
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,800
Wait, is my cooking
really that funny?

294
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:29,870
Come on, what's so funny about this?

295
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:41,490
It really does taste bizarre.

296
00:19:41,650 --> 00:19:43,950
It tastes like my stomach
is bursting into laughter.

297
00:19:44,690 --> 00:19:47,120
Who messes around
with food like this?

298
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,690
You're the worst one of all, Mom.

299
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:51,360
You're just as bad, Dad.

300
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:52,730
Even at my kindergarten,

301
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:55,130
we get in big trouble
if we mess around with food.

302
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:58,300
You're worse than a child.
Just pathetic.

303
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,370
What an embarrassment
in front of Teun Teun.

304
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:19,620
No matter what anyone says,

305
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:22,190
I'm Mom and Dad's daughter.

306
00:20:24,290 --> 00:20:25,860
I'm the daughter of Cheongma.

307
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,600
Hae Ra, you're home.

308
00:20:34,910 --> 00:20:36,310
Did you drink?

309
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:43,180
What's wrong? Did something happen?

310
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:47,620
No.

311
00:20:56,890 --> 00:20:59,100
The OB-GYN clinic
where you were born?

312
00:20:59,730 --> 00:21:02,630
Yes. It's still there, right?

313
00:21:02,930 --> 00:21:04,130
Of course.

314
00:21:04,230 --> 00:21:07,700
It's probably the oldest hospital
in that area.

315
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:10,610
Why do you ask all of a sudden?

316
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:13,480
I was just curious.

317
00:21:13,810 --> 00:21:15,050
Oh, right.

318
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:18,380
About Director Joo...

319
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:22,090
How did she become
my nanny back then?

320
00:21:22,150 --> 00:21:25,190
She came for a nanny interview,

321
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:29,090
and you cried incessantly that day.

322
00:21:29,490 --> 00:21:32,630
But the moment
she held you in her arms,

323
00:21:33,430 --> 00:21:35,700
you stopped crying just like that.

324
00:21:37,430 --> 00:21:40,600
Even as your mom,
I found it amazing.

325
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:47,240
I was struggling so much back then
with postpartum depression.

326
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:51,280
So when she offered
to take care of you,

327
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:53,120
I was so grateful.

328
00:21:54,950 --> 00:21:59,090
Ever since that day,
she has lived with us.

329
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:05,660
If you hadn't cried like that,

330
00:22:07,130 --> 00:22:08,270
Director Joo...

331
00:22:08,770 --> 00:22:11,440
would never have moved in
under the same roof.

332
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:17,110
You were crying your heart out,
you see.

333
00:22:26,650 --> 00:22:30,120
But you have to promise me
you'll study abroad.

334
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:34,690
In my opinion,
there's a right time for studying.

335
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:38,330
If you put it off any longer,
it won't be easy to go.

336
00:22:42,670 --> 00:22:45,040
Why is she trying so hard
to send me away?

337
00:22:50,510 --> 00:22:53,480
I can't take her words
at face value.

338
00:23:03,850 --> 00:23:06,960
Didn't you have a scholarship foundation
meeting today?

339
00:23:09,390 --> 00:23:10,890
Whatever. I'm tired.

340
00:23:11,860 --> 00:23:13,630
Want to get dinner together then?

341
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:15,970
I checked,
and your favorite restaurant...

342
00:23:16,030 --> 00:23:17,130
still has a table open.

343
00:23:18,170 --> 00:23:21,170
No, I want to head home early.
I'm tired.

344
00:23:23,070 --> 00:23:24,440
Are you coming down with something?

345
00:23:25,810 --> 00:23:27,010
No, I'm fine.

346
00:23:29,810 --> 00:23:31,720
All right. I'll take you home then.

347
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:48,370
Right.

348
00:23:50,230 --> 00:23:51,900
That's how you really feel,
isn't it?

349
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:55,240
Maybe it's for the best.

350
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:58,480
I knew what I was getting into
from the start.

351
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:01,650
Nothing has changed.

352
00:24:18,130 --> 00:24:20,060
Anyway, enough about that.

353
00:24:23,070 --> 00:24:26,070
If you still can't believe it,
run a test against this.

354
00:24:28,370 --> 00:24:29,570
(Korea Genetic Analysis Institute)

355
00:24:54,330 --> 00:24:58,030
What if Director Joo
really turns out to be my mom?

356
00:25:03,040 --> 00:25:04,140
What are you doing here?

357
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:07,040
Nothing.

358
00:25:18,790 --> 00:25:20,820
(Cheongma)

359
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:32,200
I thought it would match
my outfit today.

360
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:35,910
As expected of a designer,
you have great taste, Eun Seol.

361
00:25:36,140 --> 00:25:37,710
What do you think?
Don't they go well together?

362
00:25:38,740 --> 00:25:39,740
They do.

363
00:25:39,910 --> 00:25:43,450
You can pull off
any accessory, Director.

364
00:25:43,980 --> 00:25:46,250
Eun Seol,
is there anything you want?

365
00:25:47,220 --> 00:25:48,990
Shall we get matching rings?

366
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:53,120
Just name it.
I'll get everything ready for you.

367
00:25:54,860 --> 00:25:56,790
May I really?

368
00:25:57,590 --> 00:25:58,830
Of course.

369
00:26:02,930 --> 00:26:06,770
Then I'd like the gloves you have on
in that photo.

370
00:26:09,670 --> 00:26:12,610
They look really pretty to me.

371
00:26:17,650 --> 00:26:20,080
Of course,
they're not really my style,

372
00:26:20,580 --> 00:26:22,820
but I want to have
the same elegance you do.

373
00:26:24,690 --> 00:26:26,590
Oh, I see.

374
00:26:27,490 --> 00:26:30,030
Well, getting those gloves
is easy enough.

375
00:26:30,390 --> 00:26:31,590
Is there anything else you want?

376
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:33,300
That's all.

377
00:26:34,530 --> 00:26:37,300
Never hesitate to ask me
for anything.

378
00:26:38,030 --> 00:26:41,570
I want to make up for everything
I couldn't do for you before.

379
00:26:50,210 --> 00:26:51,550
What should we eat today?

380
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:53,550
Gosh, Eun Seol!

381
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:57,020
Director Joo,
I see you two are together.

382
00:26:57,220 --> 00:27:00,260
If you haven't eaten yet,
let's grab lunch together.

383
00:27:01,790 --> 00:27:03,630
Forget it. I'm not interested.

384
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,200
What...

385
00:27:10,900 --> 00:27:13,000
Then, let's take a rain check.

386
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:16,570
I need to talk to Eun Seol about
the scholarship foundation anyway.

387
00:27:17,740 --> 00:27:19,040
All right, then.

388
00:27:19,610 --> 00:27:23,350
Eun Seol, let's definitely
grab a meal together next time.

389
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,880
Sure.

390
00:27:26,150 --> 00:27:27,180
Hae Ra?

391
00:27:30,620 --> 00:27:31,820
Director,

392
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:35,530
I don't think I'll be able
to join you today either.

393
00:27:36,030 --> 00:27:38,060
There's something urgent
I need to take care of.

394
00:27:39,360 --> 00:27:41,460
Sure, we'll do it next time then.

395
00:28:00,650 --> 00:28:04,790
Excuse me, is it possible
to purchase this product again?

396
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:09,590
Give me just a moment.
I'll check and let you know.

397
00:28:09,790 --> 00:28:10,790
Okay.

398
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:18,600
Welcome.

399
00:28:28,750 --> 00:28:30,780
Can I get this exact same model?

400
00:28:32,320 --> 00:28:33,320
This was...

401
00:28:33,650 --> 00:28:36,650
only offered to 100 VIPs
5 years ago,

402
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:38,150
so it isn't available
for purchase, ma'am.

403
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:41,460
Then is there anything similar?

404
00:28:41,930 --> 00:28:43,560
One moment. Let me check for you.

405
00:28:47,930 --> 00:28:49,600
The owner of these gloves...

406
00:28:50,270 --> 00:28:52,140
is really Director Joo?

407
00:28:52,540 --> 00:28:53,800
Could you please come this way?

408
00:29:04,910 --> 00:29:08,380
I think it's best to keep
your distance from Ms. Joo for now.

409
00:29:08,690 --> 00:29:10,350
Just because
she's your mother's friend...

410
00:29:10,420 --> 00:29:12,160
doesn't mean you should
let your guard down.

411
00:29:12,460 --> 00:29:14,790
(Basic Early Pregnancy Screening)

412
00:29:14,860 --> 00:29:17,160
(Mother's Name: Joo Ae Sook,
Baby DOB: September 11, 2000)

413
00:29:27,340 --> 00:29:28,370
That's right.

414
00:29:30,370 --> 00:29:32,580
The birth mother
you've been looking for...

415
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:35,450
That's...

416
00:29:36,950 --> 00:29:37,950
me.

417
00:29:41,450 --> 00:29:42,790
It's you?

418
00:29:50,860 --> 00:29:52,230
I'm sorry, Eun Seol.

419
00:29:56,930 --> 00:29:57,930
Ma'am.

420
00:29:58,130 --> 00:29:59,740
I'm sorry, but this item...

421
00:29:59,740 --> 00:30:02,770
was only offered to 100 VIPs
5 years ago,

422
00:30:03,240 --> 00:30:04,770
so it's no longer available
for purchase.

423
00:30:38,040 --> 00:30:41,840
(A Trap Called Desire)

424
00:30:42,110 --> 00:30:44,680
Because I can't just take
your word for it anymore.

425
00:30:44,810 --> 00:30:47,250
I'm your mom.
Of course I can do that much.

426
00:30:47,280 --> 00:30:50,420
If you drag my life into the mud,
you're going down with me.

427
00:30:50,490 --> 00:30:52,790
Luxury retirement homes have
great facilities these days.

428
00:30:52,860 --> 00:30:55,020
We could also assign
a dedicated caregiver.

429
00:30:55,090 --> 00:30:57,490
You're not putting your mother
in a facility, are you?

430
00:30:57,760 --> 00:31:00,400
I want to be by your side
every day too, sir.

431
00:31:00,460 --> 00:31:01,630
Just like the Chairman.

432
00:31:01,760 --> 00:31:03,530
Daughter, don't you miss your dad?

433
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:06,370
You're going to be the next head
of Cheongma, after all.

434
00:31:06,570 --> 00:31:08,070
It's not true, right?
Tell me it's not true.

435
00:31:08,140 --> 00:31:10,040
There's no way
you could be my mother.

436
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:12,810
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
